"KRONOS 2310 titanium dioxide - KRONOS Worldwide, Inc (https://www.kronosww.com/grade/kronos-2310/)\nciteturn41search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # KRONOS 2310 ... Oil absorption (DIN EN ISO 787-5)*  |  | 18 g/100 g pigment ... Since 1916, KRONOS ® has been producing titanium dioxide pigments (TiO_{2}), the world’s primary pigment for providing whiteness, brightness, and opacity.\n\n# KRONOS 2310\n\nZirconia-treated rutile pigment with outstanding optical properties for all demanding exterior coatings\n\nDownload\n\nList of product grades\n\n## Applications\n\n  * Architectural Coatings\n  * Coil coatings and UV-cured finishes\n  * Powder coatings\n  * Waterborne paints\n  * High-quality industrial coatings\n  * Screen and digital printing inks\n  * White and tinted automotive finishes and vehicle refinish systems\n\n## Properties\n\n  * Imparts maximum brightness and a neutral tone in white coatings\n  * Produces brilliant, clean tints\n  * Disperses readily and meets all requirements of modern production methods\n  * Delivers very high opacity making it economical in use\n  * Produces glossy, low-haze coatings\n  * Is suitable for all exterior paints and coatings\n\n\n## Product characteristics\n\nProduction  |  | rutile pigment produced by the chloride process\nSurface treatment  |  | aluminum, silicon and zirconium compounds\nTiO_{2} content (DIN EN ISO 591)  |  | ≥ 93.9%\nStandard classification (DIN EN ISO 591-1)  |  | R 2\nASTM D 476  |  | Type II, III, VI & VII\nDensity (DIN EN ISO 787-10)*  |  | 4.0 g/cm^{3}\nBulking value*  |  | 0.25 l/kg (0.03 gal/lb)\nOil absorption (DIN EN ISO 787-5)*  |  | 18 g/100 g pigment\nColor index  |  | Pigment White 6 (77891)\nCAS No.  |  | 13463-67-7\nREACH Registration No.  |  | 01-2119489379-17-xxxx\n\n\n## Related products\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\n2310 KRONOS 2310 TMP- and TME-free (Type 3752). For coatings with outstanding optical properties and very high weathering performance.\n\n+ Add to compare\n\n2300 Versatile rutile pigment with excellent optical properties and dispersibility for various indoor coatings\n\n+ Add to compare\n\n2360 Rutile pigment with superior weather durability for architectural and industrial coatings and colored PVC profiles\n\n+ Add to compare\n\n2160 Rutile pigment with highest weather durability for powder and coil coatings and colored PVC profiles\n\n+ Add to compare\n\n2190 Rutile pigment free of TMP and TME with high gloss and outstanding opacity for various paint and coating systems\n\n+ Add to compare\n\nCompare\n\nSince 1916, KRONOS ® has been producing titanium dioxide pigments (TiO_{2}), the world’s primary pigment for providing whiteness, brightness, and opacity.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTMP- and TME-free Grades - KRONOS Worldwide, Inc (https://www.kronosww.com/page_part/tmp-and-tme-free-grades/)\nciteturn41search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; KRONOS 2190 and KRONOS 2310 free of TMP- and TME (Type 3752) are the first in a series of reinvented TiO_{2} pigments addressing emerging product stewardship aspects without affecting the optical and physical performance of the pigment in coatings systems. ... Since 1916, KRONOS ® has been producing titanium dioxide pigments (TiO_{2}), the world’s primary pigment for providing whiteness, brightness, and opacity.\n\n## TMP- and TME-free Grades\n\nKRONOS 2190 and KRONOS 2310 free of TMP- and TME (Type 3752) are the first in a series of reinvented TiO_{2} pigments addressing emerging product stewardship aspects without affecting the optical and physical performance of the pigment in coatings systems.\n\nThe new KRONOS TMP- and TME-free grades exhibit similar performance to the TMP-version in waterborne, solvent-based and powder coatings and are already successfully used by our coatings customers.\n\n## Why TMP-free\n\nAchieving the ecolabel requirements in Europe\n\nKRONOS developed trimethylolpropane (TMP)-free alternatives of these successful pigment grades to address a recent regulatory self-classification of TMP by its manufacturer, even though our original coating grades contain an amount of TMP below regulatory thresholds.\n\n## Applications\n\nIn our relentless drive to continuously improve, we have introduced new products to address new and emerging product stewardship aspects. The new TMP-free versions meet the high-quality standards of our KRONOS product portfolio.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKronos 2310 – Kronos TiO₂ | TiO₂ Wiki (https://www.tio2.wiki/products/kronos-2310)\nciteturn41search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # Kronos 2310 ... Oil Absorption  | 22-28  | g/100g  | ISO 787-5 ... ## Similar or Equivalent Grades\n\n# Kronos 2310\n\nRutile Chloride process Kronos Germany\n\n## Overview\n\nA premium chloride-process rutile grade with dense silica/alumina treatment for maximum exterior durability.\n\n## Technical Specifications\n\nProperty  | Value  | Unit  | Test Method\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nTiO₂ Content  | ≥88  | %  | ISO 591\nBrightness (Y)  | ≥94  | %  | ISO 2469\nOil Absorption  | 22-28  | g/100g  | ISO 787-5\npH (aqueous)  | 7.5-9.5  | —  | ISO 787-9\nSpecific Gravity  | 3.8  | g/cm³  | ISO 787-10\nAverage Particle Size  | 0.31  | μm  | Electron microscopy\n\nNote: Specifications are typical values and may vary. Always confirm with current technical data sheets from the manufacturer.\n\n## Typical Applications\n\nAutomotive Coatings\n\n## Similar or Equivalent Grades\n\nThese grades have similar specifications or are commonly considered as alternatives:\n\nR-960 rutile Chemours • United States A highly durable chloride-process rutile TiO₂ designed for exterior applications with superior weathering resistance.automotive coatingsindustrial coatingsTR-93 rutile Tronox • United States A premium rutile TiO₂ with dense silica treatment for exceptional durability in exterior architectural coatings.automotive coatingsar