PAPER-D matches Kronos 2073 as a European-reference decor paper rutile.Compare →SEMITI 996 vs 2310 SEMITI 996 is universal; Kronos 2310 is plastics-focused. ... SEMITI 298 vs R-298 SEMITI 298 sources from the same LB Group tier-1 producer family as LB R-298 — functionally equivalent with trade-direct sourcing.Compare →SEMITI 996 vs R-996 SEMITI 996 is the SEMITECH-branded export-trade version of LB R-996 — same tier-1 chloride rutile, different supply structure.Compare →SEMITI 218 vs R-218 SEMITI 218 is the SEMITECH-branded version of LB R-218 sulfate coatings rutile.Compare →SEMITI 248 vs R-218P (plastics)SEMITI 248 is the plastics-tuned sulfate rutile from LB Group sourced via SEMITECH trade.Compare →\n\nCompare\n\n# SEMITI vs the global TiO2 reference brands\n\nWhen formulators evaluate substituting one TiO2 grade for another, they look at three things: matched performance specs, drop-in compatibility with existing formulations, and the cost gap. Each comparison page below answers all three for a specific SEMITI grade vs the corresponding international reference grade — with side-by-side spec tables, when-to-choose decision criteria, and pricing context.\n\n## SEMITI vs Chemours\n\nSEMITI 996 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 996 is engineered as a 1:1 drop-in substitute for Ti-Pure R-902 in coatings, plastic masterbatch, and inks.Compare →SEMITI 706 vs Ti-Pure R-706 SEMITI 706 matches Ti-Pure R-706's premium durability for industrial and automotive coatings — at 35–40% lower landed cost.Compare →SEMITI 902 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 902 is specifically engineered to drop into Ti-Pure R-902-qualified architectural paint formulations.Compare →SEMITI 706W vs Ti-Pure R-746 SEMITI 706W matches Ti-Pure R-746 as a hydrophilic-tuned rutile for waterborne architectural emulsion paints.Compare →SEMITI 960 vs Ti-Pure R-960 SEMITI 960 matches Ti-Pure R-960's amine-compatible HALS-friendly surface treatment for engineering plastics masterbatch.Compare →SEMITI INK-1 vs Ti-Pure R-931 SEMITI INK-1 matches Ti-Pure R-931 as an easy-dispersion ink-grade rutile for offset, flexo, gravure, and UV inks.Compare →SEMITI PAPER-D vs Ti-Pure R-104 SEMITI PAPER-D matches Ti-Pure R-104 as a decor and laminate paper-grade rutile.Compare →【7†SEMITI 2310 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 2310 is plastics-specific; Ti-Pure R-902 is universal coatings/plastics. \n## SEMITI vs Tronox\n\nSEMITI 826D vs CR-826 SEMITI 826D matches Tronox CR-826's industry-leading chalking resistance for coil coatings and outdoor industrial paint.Compare →SEMITI 880 vs CR-880 SEMITI 880 matches Tronox CR-880's automotive OEM acid-rain resistance and tight color tolerance.Compare →SEMITI A100 vs A-HR SEMITI A100 is sulfate-process anatase; Tronox A-HR is chloride. Different positioning — choose by cost vs absolute spec.Compare →SEMITI SL70 vs SL-70 SEMITI SL70 is a direct 70% TiO2 slurry alternative to Tronox SL-70 for waterborne paint and paper coating.Compare →SEMITI 996 vs CR-828 SEMITI 996 matches Tronox CR-828 as a universal chloride rutile for coatings, plastics, and inks.Compare →\n\n## SEMITI vs Kronos\n\nSEMITI 2310 vs 2310 SEMITI 2310 is engineered as a direct alternative to Kronos 2310 for universal plastics applications.Compare →SEMITI 2160 vs 2160 SEMITI 2160 matches Kronos 2160's outdoor PVC durability for window frames, siding, and fence boards.Compare →SEMITI 2190 vs 2190 SEMITI 2190 matches Kronos 2190 as a premium plastics rutile for engineering plastics and 20-year warranty PVC.Compare →SEMITI PAPER-D vs 2073 SEMITI PAPER-D matches Kronos 2073 as a European-reference decor paper rutile.Compare →【23†SEMITI 996 vs 2310 SEMITI 996 is universal; Kronos 2310 is plastics-focused. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKRONOS Titanium Dioxide (https://www.kronosww.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/KRONOS_List-of-Grades.pdf?v=1774111646)\nciteturn41search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; [%] | 2044 85.5 | 2047 91.0 | 2056 94.8 | 2064 96.6 